{
	"$comment": "Component registry: one entry per pattern (TypeScript + SCSS), per CSS-only component, per layout partial and per utility family, keyed by name; the inventory discovers the components, this file classifies them, and a test fails when the two disagree (npm run evals:doctor lists the differences and --fix appends derived entries). Fields: kind = tier (pattern | component | layout | utility; the directory gives the default, the registry may override it, e.g. animate and columns are helpers filed under 04-patterns); roles (patterns): provider = behaviour delegated to a provider library, overlay = opens a layer and must manage focus and Escape, composite = arrow-key widget, feedback = announces status, non-interactive = renders no control of its own, no-dom = attaches behaviour to existing elements; family: patterns that implement one keyboard model together share the parent name; host {host, reason} (components and layout): styles markup something else emits, so no markup contract of its own; story: normalised story name when it differs from the component name; title (utility families): display name in the utilities documentation; interactive (CSS-only components): operated by the user; loading / validating: has a loading or an invalid state; density: the enterprise document expects a size or density axis; derived: true when the doctor appended the entry from code signals, remove after review.",
